; Bounded four-phase request/acknowledge handshake with retries and a stop record
; (PinScript ISA candidate v0.1). A general pin handshake, not a protocol controller.
; REQ (pin 4) is open drain with an external pull-up: the engine pulls it low to
; request and releases it afterwards. ACK (pin 5) is an input with an external pull-up.
; Responder contract (assumed, not enforced):
;   R1 ACK is idle released (high) and is pulled low only in response to REQ low.
;   R2 Once ACK is asserted it stays low until the responder observes REQ released,
;      then it is released within ACK_TIMEOUT cycles.
;   R3 A responder may still assert a late ACK after a timed-out request was withdrawn
;      (a reaction already in flight); it then releases it under R2.
;   R4 The responder may keep REQ low for a while after the engine releases it
;      (busy extension); a released open-drain REQ is then observed low, never high.
; Accounted guard: before every request the program waits (bounded) for ACK to read
; high, so a stale or late ACK is never accepted as the answer to a new request.
; Residual assumption: a late ACK must not start in the four pad cycles between the
; last pad cycle the idle check sampled and the first cycle a genuine response can
; appear (synchronizer latency plus the CLR/LDT instructions). Under R3 this holds
; when BACKOFF exceeds the responder's reaction time.
.param ACK_TIMEOUT, 100      ; ACK sampled in ACK_TIMEOUT+1 consecutive cycles
.param RELEASE_TIMEOUT, 50   ; budget for REQ to read high after release
.param IDLE_TIMEOUT, 200     ; budget for ACK to read high before a request
.param ATTEMPTS, 3
.param BACKOFF, 20
.pin REQ, 4
.pin ACK, 5

        SET REQ                 ; OUT=1: released once open drain is enabled
        OPENDRAIN REQ
        DRIVE REQ
        LD R0, ATTEMPTS
attempt:
        LDT IDLE_TIMEOUT
        WAIT HI(ACK), FAULT     ; never request while ACK still reads low
        CLR REQ                 ; pull REQ low: request
        LDT ACK_TIMEOUT
        WAIT LO(ACK), retry     ; acknowledge within the budget, else retry
        SET REQ                 ; release REQ
        LDT RELEASE_TIMEOUT
        WAIT HI(REQ), FAULT     ; REQ must really rise: WAIT_TIMEOUT if held low
        LDT ACK_TIMEOUT
        WAIT HI(ACK), FAULT     ; responder must release ACK
        HALT
retry:  SET REQ                 ; withdraw the request
        DELAY BACKOFF
        DJNZ R0, attempt
        FAULT 1                 ; no acknowledge after ATTEMPTS requests
